      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we can harden this code by adding a couple of checks:\n\n1. If the vector is not empty, it must contain just one device of the type `IN_SUBMIX` (for the output stream, `OUT_SUBMIX`), otherwise log an error and return `DeviceSwitchBehavior::UNSUPPORTED_DEVICES`.\n\n2. And just as a safeguard to prevent an UB in the `StreamRemoteSubmix` constructor when taking `devices.front()`, check that if `isStubStream`, then the vector of devices must be not empty. It should be a fatal failure because this is the assumption we rely on.",
